{
  "id": 460310564,
  "iid": 23752,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "icmp: Add expert warning when code must be zero",
  "description": "Per RFC 792, RFC 1256, and RFC 950, certain ICMP message types require the Code field to be zero.\n\nThis change adds an expert warning (icmp.code.must_be_zero) when a non-zero Code value is detected for:\n\n- Echo Request / Echo Reply\n- Timestamp Request / Timestamp Reply\n- Router Solicitation\n- Address Mask Request / Reply\n\nThis improves protocol compliance validation without altering existing dissection behavior.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-03-02T17:00:28.698Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-03-10T00:37:13.268Z",
