    {
      "id": "cd6275cf6d703a8baf013a30fc69d1c4396ce6c0",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3126459270,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Good point.\n\nAfter auditing `packet-icmp.c`, I found that in addition to the currently enforced types, `ICMP_ALTHOST` and `ICMP_EXTECHO` are also implemented as Code=0-only (their code tables contain only value 0), but they are not validated with `icmp.code.must_be_zero`.\n\nThis creates inconsistency, especially since `ICMP_MASKREQ/MASKREPLY` are both deprecated and validated, while `ICMP_ALTHOST` is deprecated but not validated.\n\nI will extend the validation to all types that are effectively Code=0-only in the current implementation (including `ICMP_ALTHOST` and `ICMP_EXTECHO`) to keep the policy consistent and orthogonal to deprecation. I’ll push an update shortly.",
          "author": {
            "id": 31060610,
            "username": "urvalkheni",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Urval Kheni",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/31060610/avatar.png?v=1788515628",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/urvalkheni"
